{"id":"mahabharata-13-051","work":"mahabharata","part":13,"partName":"अनुशासनपर्व","partNameEn":"Anushasana Parva","unit":51,"title":"एकपञ्चाशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 51 · Chyavana's price and the worth of cows","summary":{"en":"King Nahusha goes with his ministers to Chyavana, who asks for a price for himself, and the king offers more and more, until the sage says that the price of a brahmin like himself is a cow. A wise old sage declares that a brahmin and a cow are of equal worth, and tells of the greatness of cows, who are the ladder of heaven.","kn":"ರಾಜ ನಹುಷ ಮಂತ್ರಿಗಳೊಡನೆ ಚ್ಯವನನ ಬಳಿ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ತನಗೆ ಬೆಲೆ ಕೇಳಿದಾಗ ರಾಜ ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಹೆಚ್ಚು ಕೊಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಕೊನೆಗೆ ತನ್ನಂತಹ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನ ಬೆಲೆ ಒಂದು ಗೋವು ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವೃದ್ಧ ಋಷಿ ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣ ಮತ್ತು ಗೋವು ಸಮಾನ ಮೌಲ್ಯವೆಂದು ಹೇಳಿ ಗೋವುಗಳು ಸ್ವರ್ಗದ ಏಣಿ ಎನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"राजा नहुष मन्त्रियों सहित च्यवन के पास जाते हैं, जो अपना मूल्य माँगते हैं, और राजा बढ़ाते जाते हैं, अन्त में ऋषि कहते हैं कि उन जैसे ब्राह्मण का मूल्य एक गाय है। एक बुद्धिमान वृद्ध मुनि कहते हैं कि ब्राह्मण और गौ समान मूल्य के हैं, और गौएँ स्वर्ग की सीढ़ी हैं।","te":"రాజు నహుషుడు మంత్రులతో చ్యవనుని వద్దకు వెళ్తాడు, తనకు వెల అడగగా రాజు పెంచుతూ పోతాడు, చివరకు తనలాంటి బ్రాహ్మణుని వెల ఒక ఆవు అని ఋషి అంటాడు. బ్రాహ్మణుడు, ఆవు సమాన విలువని, ఆవులు స్వర్గానికి నిచ్చెన అని ఒక వృద్ధ ఋషి చెబుతాడు.","ta":"மன்னன் நகுஷன் அமைச்சர்களுடன் சியவனரிடம் செல்ல, அவர் தமக்கு விலை கேட்க, மன்னன் கூட்டிக்கொண்டே போகிறான், இறுதியில் தம்மைப் போன்ற அந்தணனின் விலை ஒரு பசு என்கிறார் முனிவர். அந்தணனும் பசுவும் சம மதிப்புடையவர், பசுக்கள் சொர்க்கத்தின் படி என்று ஒரு முதிய முனிவர் கூறுகிறார்.","ml":"നഹുഷ രാജാവ് മന്ത്രിമാരോടൊപ്പം ച്യവനന്റെ അടുത്തെത്തുന്നു; മുനി തനിക്ക് ഒരു വില ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു, രാജാവ് കൂടുതൽ കൂടുതൽ വാഗ്ദാനം ചെയ്യുന്നു. തന്നെപ്പോലൊരു ബ്രാഹ്മണന്റെ വില ഒരു പശുവാണെന്ന് മുനി പറയുന്നു. ബ്രാഹ്മണനും പശുവും ഒരേ മൂല്യമുള്ളവരാണെന്ന് ഒരു ജ്ഞാനിയായ വൃദ്ധമുനി പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; സ്വർഗ്ഗത്തിലേക്കുള്ള ഗോവണിയായ പശുക്കളുടെ മഹത്ത്വവും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 13.51; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Nov 03 2026","sections":[{"title":"आनुशासनिकपर्व","titleEn":"Anushasanika Parva (The instructions)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"नहुषस्तु ततः श्रुत्वा च्यवनं तं तथागतम् ।\nत्वरितः प्रययौ तत्र सहामात्यपुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing that Chyavana had come to such a state, Nahusha then hurried there with his ministers and priest."}},{"n":2,"text":"शौचं कृत्वा यथान्यायं प्राञ्जलिः प्रयतो नृपः ।\nआत्मानमाचचक्षे च च्यवनाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, having purified himself properly, stood with joined palms, disciplined, and introduced himself to the great-souled Chyavana."}},{"n":3,"text":"अर्चयामास तं चापि तस्य राज्ञः पुरोहितः ।\nसत्यव्रतं महाभागं देवकल्पं विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king's priest also honored him, lord of the people, the greatly blessed sage of true vows, who was like a god."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":4,"text":"करवाणि प्रियं किं ते तन्मे व्याख्यातुमर्हसि ।\nसर्वं कर्तास्मि भगवन्यद्यपि स्यात्सुदुष्करम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"What can I do to please you? Please tell me. Venerable one, I will do it all, even if it is very hard."}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"श्रमेण महता युक्ताः कैवर्ता मत्स्यजीविनः ।\nमम मूल्यं प्रयच्छैभ्यो मत्स्यानां विक्रयैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"These fishermen, who live by fish, have labored greatly. Pay them my price, along with the price of the fish they would sell."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"सहस्रं दीयतां मूल्यं निषादेभ्यः पुरोहित ।\nनिष्क्रयार्थं भगवतो यथाह भृगुनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Priest, let a thousand be given to the fishermen as the price for the venerable one's ransom, as the Bhrigu's descendant has asked."}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"सहस्रं नाहमर्हामि किं वा त्वं मन्यसे नृप ।\nसदृशं दीयतां मूल्यं स्वबुद्ध्या निश्चयं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am not worth a thousand. What do you think, king? Give a fitting price; decide by your own judgment."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":8,"text":"सहस्राणां शतं क्षिप्रं निषादेभ्यः प्रदीयताम् ।\nस्यादेतत्तु भवेन्मूल्यं किं वान्यन्मन्यते भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let a hundred thousand be quickly given to the fishermen. Would that be the price, or do you think of something else?"}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"नाहं शतसहस्रेण निमेयः पार्थिवर्षभ ।\nदीयतां सदृशं मूल्यममात्यैः सह चिन्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot be measured by a hundred thousand, best of kings. Give a fitting price; consider it with your ministers."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":10,"text":"कोटिः प्रदीयतां मूल्यं निषादेभ्यः पुरोहित ।\nयदेतदपि नौपम्यमतो भूयः प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Priest, give the fishermen a crore as the price. If even this is not comparable, let more be given."}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"राजन्नार्हाम्यहं कोटिं भूयो वापि महाद्युते ।\nसदृशं दीयतां मूल्यं ब्राह्मणैः सह चिन्तय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Radiant king, I am not worth a crore or more. Give a fitting price; consider it with brahmins."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"अर्धराज्यं समग्रं वा निषादेभ्यः प्रदीयताम् ।\nएतन्मूल्यमहं मन्ये किं वान्यन्मन्यसे द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let half the kingdom, or the whole of it, be given to the fishermen. I think that is the price. Or do you think of something else, brahmin?"}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"अर्धराज्यं समग्रं वा नाहमर्हामि पार्थिव ।\nसदृशं दीयतां मूल्यमृषिभिः सह चिन्त्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am not worth half a kingdom or the whole of it, king. Give a fitting price; take counsel with sages."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"महर्षेर्वचनं श्रुत्वा नहुषो दुःखकर्शितः ।\nस चिन्तयामास तदा सहामात्यपुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the great sage's words, Nahusha, wasted with distress, then thought it over with his ministers and priest."}},{"n":15,"text":"तत्र त्वन्यो वनचरः कश्चिन्मूलफलाशनः ।\nनहुषस्य समीपस्थो गविजातोऽभवन्मुनिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then another sage, a forest dweller who ate roots and fruits and had been born of a cow, came and stood near Nahusha."}},{"n":16,"text":"स समाभाष्य राजानमब्रवीद्द्विजसत्तमः ।\nतोषयिष्याम्यहं विप्रं यथा तुष्टो भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of brahmins addressed the king and said: I will satisfy the brahmin so that he will be pleased."}},{"n":17,"text":"नाहं मिथ्यावचो ब्रूयां स्वैरेष्वपि कुतोऽन्यथा ।\nभवतो यदहं ब्रूयां तत्कार्यमविशङ्कया ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not speak falsehood even in jest, so how could I otherwise? Whatever I tell you, you must do without hesitation."}},{"text":"नहुष उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said:"}},{"n":18,"text":"ब्रवीतु भगवान्मूल्यं महर्षेः सदृशं भृगोः ।\nपरित्रायस्व मामस्माद्विषयं च कुलं च मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let the venerable one name the price that suits the great sage of the Bhrigu line. Save me, my country and my family from this."}},{"n":19,"text":"हन्याद्धि भगवान्क्रुद्धस्त्रैलोक्यमपि केवलम् ।\nकिं पुनर्मां तपोहीनं बाहुवीर्यपरायणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger the venerable one could destroy even the three worlds, let alone me, who have no austerity and rely on the strength of my arm."}},{"n":20,"text":"अगाधेऽम्भसि मग्नस्य सामात्यस्य सहर्त्विजः ।\nप्लवो भव महर्षे त्वं कुरु मूल्यविनिश्चयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be a raft, great sage, for me who am sunk in unfathomable water with my ministers and priests. Decide the price."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":21,"text":"नहुषस्य वचः श्रुत्वा गविजातः प्रतापवान् ।\nउवाच हर्षयन्सर्वानमात्यान्पार्थिवं च तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Nahusha's words, the mighty cow-born sage spoke, cheering all the ministers and the king."}},{"n":22,"text":"अनर्घेया महाराज द्विजा वर्णमहत्तमाः ।\nगावश्च पृथिवीपाल गौर्मूल्यं परिकल्प्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, brahmins, the greatest of classes, cannot be priced, and neither can cows, protector of the earth. Let a cow be reckoned as the price."}},{"n":23,"text":"नहुषस्तु ततः श्रुत्वा महर्षेर्वचनं नृप ।\nहर्षेण महता युक्तः सहामात्यपुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, king, Nahusha, hearing the great sage's words, was filled with great joy, together with his ministers and priest."}},{"n":24,"text":"अभिगम्य भृगोः पुत्रं च्यवनं संशितव्रतम् ।\nइदं प्रोवाच नृपते वाचा संतर्पयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to Chyavana, the son of Bhrigu, of sharp vows, king, he said these words, as if soothing him with speech:"}},{"n":25,"text":"उत्तिष्ठोत्तिष्ठ विप्रर्षे गवा क्रीतोऽसि भार्गव ।\nएतन्मूल्यमहं मन्ये तव धर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rise, rise, brahmin sage! You are bought with a cow, descendant of Bhrigu. I take this to be your price, best of upholders of dharma."}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":26,"text":"उत्तिष्ठाम्येष राजेन्द्र सम्यक्क्रीतोऽस्मि तेऽनघ ।\nगोभिस्तुल्यं न पश्यामि धनं किंचिदिहाच्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"I rise, king of kings. I am rightly bought by you, blameless one. I see no wealth here equal to cows, unfailing one."}},{"n":27,"text":"कीर्तनं श्रवणं दानं दर्शनं चापि पार्थिव ।\nगवां प्रशस्यते वीर सर्वपापहरं शिवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, to name cows, to hear of them, to give them and even to see them is praised, hero, as removing all sins and as auspicious."}},{"n":28,"text":"गावो लक्ष्म्याः सदा मूलं गोषु पाप्मा न विद्यते ।\nअन्नमेव सदा गावो देवानां परमं हविः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cows are always the root of prosperity, and there is no sin in cows. Cows are food itself, and always the supreme offering of the gods."}},{"n":29,"text":"स्वाहाकारवषट्कारौ गोषु नित्यं प्रतिष्ठितौ ।\nगावो यज्ञप्रणेत्र्यो वै तथा यज्ञस्य ता मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The cries svaha and vashat are ever established in cows. Cows lead the sacrifice, and they are the mouth of the sacrifice."}},{"n":30,"text":"अमृतं ह्यक्षयं दिव्यं क्षरन्ति च वहन्ति च ।\nअमृतायतनं चैताः सर्वलोकनमस्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They pour out and carry imperishable divine nectar. They are the abode of nectar, bowed to by all the worlds."}},{"n":31,"text":"तेजसा वपुषा चैव गावो वह्निसमा भुवि ।\nगावो हि सुमहत्तेजः प्राणिनां च सुखप्रदाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In brilliance and body, cows on earth are like fire. Cows are great radiance and give happiness to living beings."}},{"n":32,"text":"निविष्टं गोकुलं यत्र श्वासं मुञ्चति निर्भयम् ।\nविराजयति तं देशं पाप्मानं चापकर्षति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The place where a herd of cows settles and breathes fearlessly shines, and sin is driven out of it."}},{"n":33,"text":"गावः स्वर्गस्य सोपानं गावः स्वर्गेऽपि पूजिताः ।\nगावः कामदुघा देव्यो नान्यत्किंचित्परं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cows are the stairway to heaven, and are honored even in heaven. Cows are goddesses who yield desires; nothing higher is remembered."}},{"n":34,"text":"इत्येतद्गोषु मे प्रोक्तं माहात्म्यं पार्थिवर्षभ ।\nगुणैकदेशवचनं शक्यं पारायणं न तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the greatness of cows that I have told you, best of kings. It speaks of only one part of their qualities; it cannot be told to the end."}},{"text":"निषादा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The fishermen said:"}},{"n":35,"text":"दर्शनं कथनं चैव सहास्माभिः कृतं मुने ।\nसतां सप्तपदं मित्रं प्रसादं नः कुरु प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sage, we have seen you and spoken with you. Friendship with the good is made in seven steps. Lord, show us favor."}},{"n":36,"text":"हवींषि सर्वाणि यथा ह्युपभुङ्क्ते हुताशनः ।\nएवं त्वमपि धर्मात्मन्पुरुषाग्निः प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As fire consumes all offerings, so you, righteous one, are a mighty fire among men."}},{"n":37,"text":"प्रसादयामहे विद्वन्भवन्तं प्रणता वयम् ।\nअनुग्रहार्थमस्माकमियं गौः प्रतिगृह्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learned one, we bow to you and seek to please you. For our benefit, please accept this cow."}},{"text":"च्यवन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Chyavana said:"}},{"n":38,"text":"कृपणस्य च यच्चक्षुर्मुनेराशीविषस्य च ।\nनरं समूलं दहति कक्षमग्निरिव ज्वलन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gaze of a wretched man, of a sage, and of a venomous snake burns a man to the root, like fire blazing through dry grass."}},{"n":39,"text":"प्रतिगृह्णामि वो धेनुं कैवर्ता मुक्तकिल्बिषाः ।\nदिवं गच्छत वै क्षिप्रं मत्स्यैर्जालोद्धृतैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fishermen, freed of sin, I accept your cow. Go quickly to heaven with the fish drawn up in the net."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"ततस्तस्य प्रसादात्ते महर्षेर्भावितात्मनः ।\nनिषादास्तेन वाक्येन सह मत्स्यैर्दिवं ययुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then by the grace of that great sage of refined soul, and by those words, the fishermen went to heaven with the fish."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततः स राजा नहुषो विस्मितः प्रेक्ष्य धीवरान् ।\nआरोहमाणांस्त्रिदिवं मत्स्यांश्च भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Nahusha, amazed, watched the fishermen and the fish ascending to heaven, bull of the Bharatas."}},{"n":42,"text":"ततस्तौ गविजश्चैव च्यवनश्च भृगूद्वहः ।\nवराभ्यामनुरूपाभ्यां छन्दयामासतुर्नृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the cow-born sage and Chyavana, the Bhrigu's descendant, offered the king fitting boons."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततो राजा महावीर्यो नहुषः पृथिवीपतिः ।\nपरमित्यब्रवीत्प्रीतस्तदा भरतसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty king Nahusha, lord of the earth, said joyfully, best of the Bharatas: Excellent."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततो जग्राह धर्मे स स्थितिमिन्द्रनिभो नृपः ।\nतथेति चोदितः प्रीतस्तावृषी प्रत्यपूजयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that king, like Indra, took his stand in dharma and, urged with So be it, honored both sages gladly."}},{"n":45,"text":"समाप्तदीक्षश्च्यवनस्ततोऽगच्छत्स्वमाश्रमम् ।\nगविजश्च महातेजाः स्वमाश्रमपदं ययौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"His vow complete, Chyavana then went to his own hermitage, and the greatly radiant cow-born sage went to his."}},{"n":46,"text":"निषादाश्च दिवं जग्मुस्ते च मत्स्या जनाधिप ।\nनहुषोऽपि वरं लब्ध्वा प्रविवेश पुरं स्वकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The fishermen and those fish went to heaven, lord of the people, and Nahusha, having received his boon, entered his own city."}},{"n":47,"text":"एतत्ते कथितं तात यन्मां त्वं परिपृच्छसि ।\nदर्शने यादृशः स्नेहः संवासे च युधिष्ठिर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you, dear son, what you asked me: what kind of affection arises from seeing and from living together."}},{"n":48,"text":"महाभाग्यं गवां चैव तथा धर्मविनिश्चयम् ।\nकिं भूयः कथ्यतां वीर किं ते हृदि विवक्षितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have told you too the greatness of cows and the settlement of dharma. What more shall I tell, hero? What do you wish to say from your heart?"}}]}]}